---
import Section from './Section.astro';
// Move 2. The one idea the whole site turns on, stated plainly, once. It earns
// move 3 (the finding) and move 4 (the product). No section-label eyebrow: the
// heading says the thing.
---

<Section id="setup">
  <h2 class="h2 reveal" style="max-width:20ch">A closed alert is a fact about the diff.</h2>

  <p class="reveal mt-8 text-[19px] leading-[1.55] lg:text-[21px]" style="--reveal-delay:60ms;max-width:60ch">
    It is not a fact about the hole. The scanner only re-checks the one thing the patch was
    written to satisfy, so it almost always goes quiet. Whether the vulnerability actually
    closed is a different question, and nothing in that loop asks it.
  </p>

  <blockquote class="reveal mt-12 border-l-2 border-accent pl-6 lg:mt-14 lg:pl-8" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">
    <p class="font-display text-[22px] font-bold leading-[1.3] tracking-[-0.018em] lg:text-[27px]" style="max-width:28ch">
      &ldquo;The alert turning green and the bug being fixed are two different events.
      The industry measures the first one.&rdquo;
    </p>
  </blockquote>
</Section>
